{title: Spring of Water}
{subtitle: John 4:13–14}
{key: D}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [D] | [Bm7] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Everyone who [D]drinks this water
Will be thirsty a[Bm7]gain
You asked for [G]a simple cup
From the deep and old [D]well
But I hold a greater [Bm7]gift
That Jacob ne[G]ver knew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Whoever drinks the wa[D]ter I give
Will never thirst a[Bm7]gain
It becomes a spring in[G]side
Welling up to life
A fountain flowing [Bm7]fresh
For [A]those who [G]stay and hear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The well is deep and [D]hard to draw
Your bucket hangs on a [Bm7]rope
But this water does [G]not run out
It wells up from [D]within
No more walking to [Bm7]the well
No more [G]heavy loads
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Whoever drinks the wa[D]ter I give
Will never thirst a[Bm7]gain
It becomes a spring in[G]side
Welling up to life
A fountain flow[Bm7]ing fresh
For [A]those who [G]stay and hear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Give me this [Bm7]water I [A]pray
So I [D]do not get thir[G]sty
So [Bm7]I do not keep [A]coming back
To [G]draw what fades away
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
A spring of wa[D]ter
To eternal [Bm7]life
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bm7] | [G] | [G] | [D] |
